---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
---
<Base title="Terms | Nimbuy" description="Terms of use for the Nimbuy website and free listing check, and how paid work is scoped.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="label">Legal</p>
      <h1>Terms</h1>
      <p style="margin-top:1rem;font-size:0.9rem">Last updated 2 October 2026</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="prose legal">
        <h2>The free check and this site</h2>
        <p>The check scores the listing text you paste using fixed word and field checks. It is an independent read by Nimbuy. It is <strong>not an AWS rating</strong> and does not predict AWS approval, search placement, ranking, sales or any business result. A score describes the text you entered at the moment you entered it.</p>
        <p>The market figures come from aggregated public AWS Marketplace listing data and describe those listings at the snapshot date shown. They are not statements about any individual product or company.</p>

        <h2>Paid work</h2>
        <p>Paid work is governed by the written scope you receive and approve before paying. The scope states what is included, what is not, the price and the dates. If something is not in the scope, it is not part of the work.</p>
        <p>Listing copy is written only from facts you provide and can evidence. You remain responsible for the accuracy of the claims in your listing and for meeting AWS Marketplace's own requirements.</p>

        <h2>No warranty, limited liability</h2>
        <p>The site and its tools are provided as they are. To the extent the law allows, Nimbuy is not liable for indirect or consequential loss arising from use of the site, the check or the guidance.</p>

        <h2>Trademarks and independence</h2>
        <p>AWS and AWS Marketplace are trademarks of Amazon.com, Inc. or its affiliates. Nimbuy is independent and is not affiliated with, endorsed by or sponsored by AWS. Other names belong to their owners.</p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>Questions: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. See also the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
